  "details": "Currently, if you have a large integer like 22121111, and use a parameter driver to copy it to another parameter, it will instead become 22121112\n\nMy guess why this is happening is that there is a float conversion going on that shouldnt be, as both the source and destination here are integers, so it should be direct\n\nI understand this is not in the 0-255 range that can be used to sync parameters, but having large numbers like this is useful for calculations, and this behaviour makes no sense",
